mod main;

// expect: E0975

/*
 * A program whose only `main` has a form the runtime cannot call (W1015 in
 * analysis). Code generation refuses it with E0975 AT that `main` - "this
 * program has no `main` function" would be wrong, and would say nothing of
 * where to look. Its help names `-c` (compile without an executable), not
 * "without -o": without -o the compiler still writes `out`.
 */
def main(count: _int64) : string { return "" + count; }
